tools.description:
Execute a batch of scene editing commands as a single call. The whole batch is preflighted first: a command that would definitely fail (unknown object/component type or property name, contradictory move_object params) rejects the batch atomically 鈥?nothing executes, and the error lists every violation. Execution is fail-fast: if a command fails at runtime, remaining commands are skipped; operations completed before the failure are preserved and the failing operation is rolled back. HARD PRECONDITION: before any construction-start command (creating/importing objects, resources, scripts, materials, prefabs, or render groups), save a valid game/general scene contract with save_plan. Read skills/Planning/SKILL.md first. Local tuning that preserves an existing contract may continue without replacing the plan. Supports alias/$ref for cross-command references.

When the batch contains add_script / import_glsl commands, compile/import logs are automatically collected and returned in `_compileCheck` 鈥?no need to call get_script_logs separately.

For preview interactions (screenshot, touch, drag, wait, reset_preview, start_preview_record, stop_preview_record, record_preview_video_mp4, pause_preview, resume_preview, transport_preview_property), use interact_by_dsl instead.

Example:
EditByDsl({
  intention: "Add a cube and set its position",
  commands: [
    {
      "commandType": "add_builtin_object",
      "params": { "object_type": "Cube" },
      "alias": "cube"
    },
    {
      "commandType": "set_component",
      "params": {
        "guid": { "$ref": "cube", "componentType": "Transform" },
        "properties": [...]
      }
    }
  ]
})
